{"id": "EUVD-2026-27650", "enisaUuid": "994c0261-5f60-37ab-9492-b4f5836f4d12", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/irdma: Fix double free related to rereg_user_mr\n\nIf IB_MR_REREG_TRANS is set during rereg_user_mr, the\numem will be released and a new one will be allocated\nin irdma_rereg_mr_trans. If any step of irdma_rereg_mr_trans\nfails after the new umem is allocated, it releases the umem,\nbut does not set iwmr->region to NULL. The problem is that\nthis failure is propagated to the user, who will then call\nibv_dereg_mr (as they should). Then, the dereg_mr path will\nsee a non-NULL umem and attempt to call ib_umem_release again.\n\nFix this by setting iwmr->region to NULL after ib_umem_release.\n\nFixed: 5ac388db27c4 (\"RDMA/irdma: Add support to re-register a memory region\")", "datePublished": "2026-05-06T07:40:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:06:14", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/62298a48f8b8788ad8b8464e6ffdf1ddebd2217e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/66964118f1f50ed85001c8fc9f7ab5bbdd021ee0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f22c32141acdcda266b26cab2b830baf870f3e0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0c5d70bcb9d2275a1c8515a924016fcfeb4ab441", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29a3edd7004bb635d299fb9bc6f0ea4ef13ed5a2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-74jp-62v9-rvjf", "CVE-2026-43120"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "18fe6066-7c36-3a5b-aca2-6bb91c324604", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac388db27c443dadfbb0b8b23fa7ccf429d901a <0c5d70bcb9d2275a1c8515a924016fcfeb4ab441"}, {"id": "1d6874f6-7b5e-3ca5-8b3e-680163455b54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "26c79f90-6299-3052-aee8-3a12c85e9ed7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac388db27c443dadfbb0b8b23fa7ccf429d901a <0f22c32141acdcda266b26cab2b830baf870f3e0"}, {"id": "2871f9dd-3522-3bb7-8ff0-a451b67e3037", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac388db27c443dadfbb0b8b23fa7ccf429d901a <66964118f1f50ed85001c8fc9f7ab5bbdd021ee0"}, {"id": "304468cb-7b3c-378b-9a2f-90766842e4af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3b0adcce-61b1-3796-8d29-54d14e08072e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.120 <6.6.136"}, {"id": "7e7ac68f-3922-3d98-b7c5-87417593ee81", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.83"}, {"id": "a4ee9dbd-a0c5-39a2-bd5a-578d9f16e702", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac388db27c443dadfbb0b8b23fa7ccf429d901a <29a3edd7004bb635d299fb9bc6f0ea4ef13ed5a2"}, {"id": "a6f652b4-c07c-3a2b-b0cc-af8b818d7a75", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "715fdb3b30541cc8180b7cdc6aa9f8c307afdf25 <62298a48f8b8788ad8b8464e6ffdf1ddebd2217e"}, {"id": "ada956a6-634d-37df-b041-6b4a51bf67f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.24"}, {"id": "b1681eb1-dd31-382f-8d9a-0f64c288dcb9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}, {"id": "b46c1ac5-ad6e-3140-adb9-5e0df812bb78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.14"}, {"id": "e256592f-0274-31c3-ab85-93f6aedfe3b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.136"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e8df8b11-57dd-34f6-8e89-89eb8123ebbe", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}